    "updated_at": "2020-09-29T15:50:57Z",
    "body": "Two options (which I think should apply to both HTML and DOM, whichever way we decide):\r\n\r\n- Keep \"Part of the revision history ... repository\" in acknowledgments, and add a separate sentence such as \"Some content is derived from the w3c/webcomponents repository, which is available under...\" in the IPR section.\r\n\r\n- Move the entire sentence into the IPR section.\r\n\r\n(Relatedly, it seems HTML could probably due to cite some more licenses, e.g. ResponsiveImagesCG/picture-element has a license that wants folks to cite it... and the custom elements [license](https://www.w3.org/Consortium/Legal/2015/copyright-software-and-document) seems to have changed its name and has rather specific suggestions for how to cite which we aren't fully following... hmm.)",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
